  "description": "Create and maintain Scoop bucket manifests (appname.json inside a bucket directory) for Windows apps, plus the install, verification, health-check and troubleshooting work that surrounds them. Use this skill whenever the user says \"create a scoop manifest\", \"write a manifest for that app\", \"add this to my bucket\", \"submit a PR to scoop-extras / main / versions\", \"write checkver / autoupdate\", \"is this app packaged yet / how do I install it\", \"the packages in my bucket are outdated / the hash is wrong / audit this bucket\", \"sync with BucketTemplate / bump GitHub Actions\", or \"scoop errors out / won't install / extraction fails / missing hash / package not found / downloads are slow\" - even if they never say the word \"scoop\". Trigger on anything involving Windows app manifests (NSIS .exe / MSI / portable .zip), bucket repositories, portable software installation, or Scoop's own configuration and troubleshooting. Projects that only ship macOS/Linux artifacts are out of scope.",
